# - Each encoded value is the mean over five independently trained PhysNet models; the run and model stand for that set of five. The ensemble results (PhysNet-ens5) are not encoded.
# - Dipole-moment and charge errors (Tables 6 and 7) and the per-atom energy MAE of Table 7 (0.054 kcal/mol) are not encoded.
# - QM9 results at smaller training sizes (100,000: 0.19; 50,000: 0.30 kcal/mol) are not encoded.
# - The residual-block counts of Table 1 (atomic 2, interaction 3, output 1) are not encoded as settings; N_module = 5 is encoded as mlips:numLayers.
# - Loss weights w_E, w_F are defined in the paper but their values were not captured; the software implementation is not named in the parts read.
# - No computational cost is reported.
# - Values of other models quoted in the tables (SchNet, DTNN, HIP-NN, GDML, enn-s2s) are literature values and are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

